      )SIC

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #82): decode_int()'s overflow check used to
      ⍝ track a parallel double-precision shadow of the exact int64
      ⍝ computation, comparing it against the conservative
      ⍝ LARGE_INT/SMALL_INT margin -- so a decode landing in the top
      ⍝ ~0.4% of the int64 range (like 2^63-1 here) was wrongly declared
      ⍝ "overflowed" and recomputed as an imprecise float even though
      ⍝ the exact integer result fits.
